# The door swinging the other way: a companion who has had enough of this
# company asks to be let go.
#
# ONE shared scene for all of them, like part_ways, with {NPC} carrying
# whichever name it is. Fires as an initiation when affinity has gone cold,
# so it is always earned: nobody walks out on a company that has treated
# them decently.
#
# The player is not helpless and is not entitled either. Persuasion can buy
# a stay, ONCE, and the DC is high because talking somebody out of leaving
# is not the same as giving them a reason to stay. Refuse to engage and
# they go.
#
# Whatever happens here, the affinity that caused it is still there
# afterward. A stay bought with words and nothing else will be asked for
# again.
#
# {PLAYER} is whoever they decided to say it to.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_PartWaysAsk

== start ==
{NPC} is waiting where {PLAYER} was going to be, which takes planning, and does not look comfortable about it.

"A word. It will not take long and you will not enjoy it."

* "Say it." -> say
* "Whatever it is, say it plainly." -> say

== say ==
"I want out."

They let that stand on its own for a moment.

"Not this minute, not in the middle of a road, and not without giving you the chance to talk me out of it. But I have been counting up what this company has been to me lately, and the number is not one I would sign for again."

* "What would it take?" -> what
* "Then go. I will not hold anybody." -> release
* "You are needed." -> needed

== needed ==
"I know. That is not the same as being wanted, and I have had a long time on this road to learn the difference."

* "What would it take?" -> what
* "Then go." -> release

== what ==
They think about that properly, which is the first hopeful thing in this conversation.

"I do not know. That is the honest answer. If you have something, say it now, because I have already packed once in my head and the second time is easier."

* [Say the thing that keeps them.] -> plead
    check Persuasion 13 -> stay | plead_bad
* "I do not have anything. You have the right to do as you please." -> release
* [Say nothing, and let them decide.] -> release

== plead ==
{PLAYER} does not argue the case. Arguing would lose it.

* [Continue.] -> stay

== stay ==
Whatever gets said, it is not a promise and it is not flattery, and it lands.

{NPC} looks at the ground for a while.

"...Right," they say at last. "Right. I will hold to that, and I will hold you to it, and I would rather not have this conversation twice."

They pick their pack back up.

"Do not make me have it twice."

* [Leave them be.] -> end
    do flag(TSC_PartWaysTalkedRound); affinity(+10); grant_xp(50)

== plead_bad ==
It is the wrong thing, said in the wrong order, and everyone standing there hears it land badly.

{NPC} nods, slowly, the way people do when a decision stops being difficult.

"That is about what I expected. No hard feelings. Genuinely."

* [Let them go.] -> release

== release ==
No speech. They were ready before this started; that was the whole point of asking.

They square the pack, check the straps twice out of habit, and look around the camp once at the people rather than the ground.

"I will hear how it ends," they say. "Everybody will."

* [Watch them go.] -> end
    do part_ways()
